{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3127","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3127","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3127\",\"parent_revision\":\"559b814d11036d8bb20cb99878c821621ac0d0cb337d24f2e6d8ca9b607aff0c\",\"root_revision\":\"559b814d11036d8bb20cb99878c821621ac0d0cb337d24f2e6d8ca9b607aff0c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nConfirmed root cause (read directly from backlog_core/server.py's _read_gate_token and backlog_add): the gate_token file is written per session ID at ~/.dh/sessions/{session_id}/.gate-token by the skill's load-time hook, and backlog_add compares the caller's token against whatever is currently in that file. When multiple subagents dispatched within one top-level session (a normal, common dispatch pattern in this plugin) each independently load the dh:work-backlog-item skill concurrently, they share the same session ID and race to overwrite the same token file \u2014 only the last writer's token still matches by the time any of them calls backlog_add. Observed directly: 8 of 9 parallel dh:task-worker subagents filing backlog items in one dispatch batch hit \\\"Direct backlog_add calls are not permitted\\\" despite passing the exact token their own skill load injected, and all 8 had to fall back to the CLI path to complete their write.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The repo owner has already indicated a preference to remove the gate_token enforcement mechanism entirely rather than fix the race, on the grounds that (1) the CLI path it is meant to funnel callers away from already has zero enforcement by design (a documented accepted gap), so the token was never actually closing the gap it targets, and (2) the compliance actually observed in this session came from the create workflow's own written instructions, not from the token blocking anything.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **mcp backlog_add gate_token check races and fails under concurrent subagent sessions** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation - #3060 incident investigation, parallel backlog-filing dispatch on 2026-08-22\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"635fffa2bc3766e14de1f82e00bd774168902ecf51a6637120e038769fbf42b2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQKqouA\"}"}